{
  "about": "Cases for comparing the rules planner with the LLM planner (financial_analyst_agent.planner_evaluation). 'scorecard' cases are the scorecard's questions; 'dev' cases are paraphrases written for the first comparison and labelled before either planner was run on them; they were held out then, and the planner changes that followed were diagnosed on them, so they are now development cases. Later development cases are in planner-cases-v2.json and planner-cases-v3.json, and the held-out cases in planner-cases-held-out-4.json. Each case is a conversation; its expectations apply to the last turn. An expectation names only what a correct answer must show: outcome (answer, clarify or refuse), intent, tickers (exactly these companies), tickers_include (at least these), metrics (exactly these), periods (kind, and count for a window), operations_include. Fields a case leaves out are not scored. Missing data is not a planning error: a refusal for a fact the recorded filings lack (codes unsupported_quarterly_fact, missing_fact) counts as outcome no_data, which satisfies an expected answer; growth shown as year-over-year rows counts as the year_over_year operation.",
